            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0979" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/258: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-01-03T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:13 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your no. 299, December 28, 4 p.m. It is the opinion of Mr. Barnes Moss that he
                    will have the situation well in hand with the new Cabinet and therefore that it
                    would serve no good purpose to send a note of that kind at present. I shall not
                    present the note before it seems necessary unless I am instructed otherwise.
                    Have mailed to Tokyo a copy of this telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
